<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John C. Frémont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a>–<a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as John Charles Frémont</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John C. Frémont was an American explorer, army officer and politician whose expeditions mapped much of the American West in the 1840s. In 1846 he encouraged the Bear Flag revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california-battalion">California Battalion</a> in its conquest. He later served as a senator for California, was the first Republican candidate for president in 1856 and was a Union general in the Civil War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-c-fremont.jpg" alt="John C. Frémont" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Charles_Fremont_Oval.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
